  <data name="TitleRansomware.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Ransomware Defense</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleRansomware.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Microsoft Defender's own Controlled Folder Access (Exploit Guard). BECETTI SECURITY only reads and explains this real Windows feature — it never runs its own ransomware engine.</value></data>
  <data name="ElevationRequiredInfoBar.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Administrator required</value></data>
  <data name="ElevationRequiredInfoBar.Message" xml:space="preserve"><value>Changing Controlled Folder Access requires an administrator. Use Settings → Restart as administrator.</value></data>
  <data name="ProtectedFoldersLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Protected folders</value></data>
  <data name="RansomwareRecommendationLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Recommendation</value></data>
  <data name="RansomwareRecommendationText.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Add your most important personal folders (Documents, Pictures, Desktop) to Controlled Folder Access from Windows Security, so ransomware cannot silently encrypt or delete them. Ask BECETTI AI if you're not sure which folders to protect.</value></data>
  <data name="EnableButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Enable</value></data>
  <data name="DisableButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Disable</value></data>

  <data name="TitlePcHealth.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Smart PC Health</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitlePcHealth.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Live CPU, memory, disk and essential-service state, read directly from Windows — nothing cached or estimated.</value></data>
  <data name="CpuUsageLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>CPU usage</value></data>
  <data name="MemoryUsageLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Memory usage</value></data>
  <data name="DisksLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Disks</value></data>
  <data name="EssentialServicesLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Essential services</value></data>

  <data name="SecurityScoreTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Security Score</value></data>

  <data name="RefreshButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Refresh</value></data>
  <data name="UninstallButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Uninstall</value></data>
  <data name="AdminRequiredInfoBar.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Administrator required</value></data>
  <data name="AdminRequiredInfoBar.Message" xml:space="preserve"><value>Changing this startup item requires an administrator. Restart BECETTI SECURITY as administrator from Settings.</value></data>

  <data name="TitleStartup.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Startup Manager</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleStartup.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Real registry startup entries — the same Run-key and Task Manager convention Windows itself uses. No performance impact score is invented: Windows does not expose one through any stable API.</value></data>

  <data name="TitleSoftware.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Software Manager</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleSoftware.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Real installed applications from the Windows registry — the same list Settings &gt; Apps shows. Uninstalling only launches the application's own real uninstaller; nothing is removed directly.</value></data>

  <data name="TitleDrivers.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Driver Monitor</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleDrivers.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Real installed device drivers from Windows (WMI), the same inventory Device Manager uses. BECETTI SECURITY has no driver issue database of its own — check Windows Update or the manufacturer's site for updates.</value></data>

  <data name="TitleUsb.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>USB Protection</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleUsb.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Real connected removable drives and Windows' own AutoPlay/AutoRun policy, which blocks the classic autorun.inf USB-malware vector. Scanning a drive runs through Microsoft Defender — BECETTI SECURITY has no USB scanning engine of its own.</value></data>
  <data name="UsbConnectedDrivesLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Connected Removable Drives</value></data>
  <data name="ScanSelectedDriveButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Scan Selected Drive with Defender</value></data>
  <data name="UsbAutoRunLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>AutoPlay / AutoRun Protection</value></data>
  <data name="EnableAutoRunProtectionButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Enable AutoRun Protection</value></data>
  <data name="DisableAutoRunProtectionButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Remove BECETTI's AutoRun Block</value></data>

  <data name="TitleNetwork.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Network Monitor</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleNetwork.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Real network adapters and active TCP connections, read from Windows' own NetworkInterface API and Get-NetTCPConnection (the same source Resource Monitor uses). BECETTI SECURITY draws no conclusion about any connection — it shows Windows' own verified list.</value></data>
  <data name="FirewallProfilesLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Firewall Profiles</value></data>
  <data name="NetworkAdaptersLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Network Adapters</value></data>
  <data name="ActiveConnectionsLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Active Connections &amp; Listening Ports</value></data>

  <data name="TitleEmergency.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Emergency Center</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleEmergency.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A single place for 'something feels wrong' moments — real status, quick access to Windows' own tools, and BECETTI AI for help.</value></data>
  <data name="QuickActionsLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Quick actions</value></data>
  <data name="OpenThreatsButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>View Threats</value></data>
  <data name="OpenWindowsSecurityButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Open Windows Security</value></data>
  <data name="OpenBackupSettingsButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Backup &amp; Recovery</value></data>
  <data name="AskBecettiAiButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Ask BECETTI AI</value></data>
  <data name="DiagnosticSummaryLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Diagnostic summary</value></data>
  <data name="DiagnosticSummaryHint.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Builds a plain-text snapshot of your current protection, firewall and PC health state for you to copy — nothing is sent anywhere automatically.</value></data>
  <data name="GenerateSummaryButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Generate Summary</value></data>

  <data name="NavVulnerability.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Vulnerability Advisor</value></data>
  <data name="TitleVulnerability.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Vulnerability Advisor</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleVulnerability.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A combined view of real checks already performed elsewhere in BECETTI SECURITY (Defender, firewall, USB AutoRun, drivers, TPM, Secure Boot, BitLocker, Windows Update). There is no separate vulnerability scanner or CVE database — every finding traces back to a named real check.</value></data>
  <data name="VulnerabilityFindingsLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Findings</value></data>

  <data name="NavBrowser.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Browser Security</value></data>
  <data name="TitleBrowser.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Browser Security</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleBrowser.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Real installed browsers (from the same installed-apps inventory Software Manager reads) and Windows' own SmartScreen policy, read from the registry.</value></data>
  <data name="SmartScreenLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>SmartScreen</value></data>
  <data name="InstalledBrowsersLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Installed Browsers</value></data>

  <data name="NavIdentity.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Identity Protection</value></data>
  <data name="TitleIdentity.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Identity Protection</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleIdentity.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Real hardware/platform security that protects your credentials and data at rest: TPM, Secure Boot, Credential Guard and BitLocker, read from Get-Tpm, Confirm-SecureBootUEFI, Win32_DeviceGuard and Get-BitLockerVolume.</value></data>

  <data name="NavWifi.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Wi-Fi Security</value></data>
  <data name="TitleWifi.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Wi-Fi Security</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleWifi.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The real authentication and cipher of the Wi-Fi network you're currently connected to, read from netsh wlan show interfaces — the same tool Windows' own Wi-Fi diagnostics use.</value></data>

  <data name="NavScheduledScan.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Scheduled Scan</value></data>
  <data name="TitleScheduledScan.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Scheduled Scan</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleScheduledScan.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Registers a real Windows Scheduled Task (visible and editable in Task Scheduler) that runs a genuine Microsoft Defender scan daily — even while BECETTI SECURITY is closed. Creating or removing it requires an administrator.</value></data>
  <data name="ScheduleNewScanLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Schedule a daily scan</value></data>
  <data name="FullScanToggle.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Full scan (otherwise Quick scan)</value></data>
  <data name="ScheduleHourLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Hour of day (0-23, local time)</value></data>
  <data name="ScheduleScanButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Schedule</value></data>
  <data name="RemoveScheduleButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Remove Scheduled Scan</value></data>

  <data name="NavBackup.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Backup Advisor</value></data>
  <data name="TitleBackup.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Backup Advisor</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleBackup.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Windows' own real backup posture: File History's service state and System Restore's real shadow copies. BECETTI SECURITY implements no backup engine of its own — antivirus protection is not a substitute for backups.</value></data>

  <data name="NavReports.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Smart Security Reports</value></data>
  <data name="TitleReports.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Smart Security Reports</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleReports.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A consolidated snapshot assembled from checks that already exist elsewhere in BECETTI SECURITY (Defender, firewall, Vulnerability Advisor). Export it as plain text or a simple PDF to share or archive.</value></data>
  <data name="SaveAsPdfButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Save as PDF</value></data>
  <data name="SaveAsTextButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Save as Text</value></data>

  <data name="NavCloudSync.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Cloud Sync</value></data>
  <data name="TitleCloudSync.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Cloud Sync</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleCloudSync.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Real connectivity and sign-in status for your BECETTI cloud account. This is a status view on top of the existing cloud sign-in — there is no second backend or data store being synchronized.</value></data>
  <data name="SyncNowButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Sync Now</value></data>

  <data name="NavKnowledge.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Knowledge Base</value></data>
  <data name="TitleKnowledge.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Knowledge Base</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleKnowledge.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Locally-authored articles explaining the real security features BECETTI SECURITY exposes and general safe-use practices. No network call is made to show this content.</value></data>
  <data name="KnowledgeSearchBox.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve"><value>Search articles...</value></data>
  <data name="SearchButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Search</value></data>

  <data name="NavThreatIntel.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Threat Intelligence</value></data>
  <data name="TitleThreatIntel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Threat Intelligence</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleThreatIntel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>An optional second opinion from VirusTotal's ~70 third-party antivirus engines for a file or link you choose — including a suspicious email attachment you saved, or a link from an email or message before you open it. This never replaces Microsoft Defender, BECETTI SECURITY's own independent protection engine — it is a separate, clearly-labelled check you run on demand.</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelNotConfiguredBar.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Not configured</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelNotConfiguredBar.Message" xml:space="preserve"><value>The threat-intelligence server is not configured. Open Settings and set the BECETTI server URL.</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelFileSectionLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Scan a file</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelScanFileButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Check hash</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelHashOnlyNote.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The file's SHA-256 is computed on this device and checked against VirusTotal's database — the file itself is not uploaded for this step.</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelUploadConsentBar.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>No existing VirusTotal report</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelUploadConsentBar.Message" xml:space="preserve"><value>This file's hash is unknown to VirusTotal. Uploading it will share the actual file content with VirusTotal and its security-industry partners, per VirusTotal's own terms. Only files up to the size shown below can be uploaded here.</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelConfirmUploadButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Upload and scan</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelUrlSectionLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Check a link</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelUrlTextBox.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve"><value>https://example.com/suspicious-link</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelScanUrlButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Scan link</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelResultLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Result</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelCheckStatusButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Check status</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelOpenReportButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Open full report on virustotal.com</value></data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelHistoryLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Previous checks</value></data>

  <data name="NavDataBreach.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Data Breach Monitor</value></data>
  <data name="TitleDataBreach.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Data Breach Monitor</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleDataBreach.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>An optional second opinion on credential exposure: check whether an email address or password has shown up in a known public data breach. This never replaces BECETTI SECURITY's own local protection — it is a separate, clearly-labelled check you run on demand.</value></data>
  <data name="DataBreachNotConfiguredBar.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Not configured</value></data>
  <data name="DataBreachNotConfiguredBar.Message" xml:space="preserve"><value>The data-breach monitoring server is not configured. Open Settings and set the BECETTI server URL.</value></data>
  <data name="DataBreachEmailSectionLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Check an email address</value></data>
  <data name="DataBreachEmailTextBox.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve"><value>name@example.com</value></data>
  <data name="DataBreachCheckEmailButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Check email</value></data>
  <data name="DataBreachRiskLabelPrefix.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Overall risk:</value></data>
  <data name="DataBreachPasswordSectionLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Check a password</value></data>
  <data name="DataBreachPasswordBox.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve"><value>Password to check</value></data>
  <data name="DataBreachPasswordPrivacyNote.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>This password is hashed on this device — only a 5-character fragment of that hash ever leaves it. The password itself is never sent or stored anywhere.</value></data>
  <data name="DataBreachCheckPasswordButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Check password</value></data>
  <data name="DataBreachHistoryLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Previous checks</value></data>

  <data name="NavIpReputation.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>IP Reputation</value></data>
  <data name="TitleIpReputation.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>IP Reputation</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleIpReputation.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>An optional second opinion on a single IP address you choose to check — for example, an unfamiliar connection you noticed in Network Monitor. Powered by AbuseIPDB's community abuse reports. This never replaces BECETTI SECURITY's own local protection.</value></data>
  <data name="IpReputationNotConfiguredBar.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Not configured</value></data>
  <data name="IpReputationNotConfiguredBar.Message" xml:space="preserve"><value>The IP reputation server is not configured. Open Settings and set the BECETTI server URL.</value></data>
  <data name="IpReputationSectionLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Check an IP address</value></data>
  <data name="IpReputationTextBox.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve"><value>203.0.113.42</value></data>
  <data name="IpReputationCheckButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Check IP</value></data>
